<p>Advocates, diaspora groups and international supporters are urging Australia to privately meet with Iran’s women’s national football team and help ensure the players’ safety after apparent signs of protest during the Women’s Asian Cup in Australia. Attention sharpened after some players declined to sing Iran’s national anthem before a match—widely seen as an act of defiance—and after at least one player appeared to make an “SOS” hand signal after a game on the Gold Coast. Iranian state media criticised the team for not singing the anthem and labelled them “wartime traitors,” language supporters say raises the risk of reprisals if the squad returns to Iran after the tournament. Community organisations and campaigners have written to Australia’s Home Affairs Minister Tony Burke seeking intervention, while some officials have stayed cautious in public, arguing that more attention could increase risks for the players and their families. The team has been staying on the Gold Coast and is due to leave Australia later this week. Calls are growing for Australian authorities to offer pathways to protection—potentially including asylum—if any players ask for it.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/AHOYtFTN-i3VNLxCgfEK8cT9HYwXeRQ1XNmRdq0UmhH6YMyaSDV7E_l4CcVKcJYkwsbLFg7QwqA5tagZf4c4-9Mzn1pe2qimUIwo6uz1JwB4IxLl-ebzldt5FiAjr1eorgfcggJ7iosSC8GGt_B4exgg57CIcWvcC51Wx43p-NVFBm4nB5eRNughgEHv0Oi38-FcabxhjfTCKkhnd02nist54cZYlUxguZ_f_bebJufRtyfbLhMWXK1gNSixCRn6Sp1DmW0zE55UTH8Cng' alt='Iran players react during the national anthem ahead of a Women’s Asian Cup match in Robina, Australia, March 8, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Private access request: AUSIRAN’s Rana Dadpour urged Australian officials to arrange private meetings with players away from “handlers” and regime-affiliated minders accompanying them in Australia.</li><li>Severity of feared reprisals: Dadpour warned the players could face extreme punishment — including execution — if they are forced to return to Iran.</li><li>Where the squad is based: Michael West Media said the team has been staying at the Royal Pines resort on the Gold Coast.</li><li>High-profile backing: Al-Monitor reported the push for protection has drawn support from politicians, human rights activists and author J.K. Rowling.</li><li>After-match tensions: Diaspora protesters surrounded the team bus after the match against Australia, and the Globe and Mail reported the team has since been eliminated from the tournament.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>AUSIRAN (women’s rights group): Founder Rana Dadpour urged Australian officials to organise private meetings with players away from “handlers” and said the women should get “every support” if they want to stay, warning of severe reprisals if they return to Iran. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/act-now-to-protect-iranian-soccer-team-australia-told/'>michaelwest.com.au</a>)</li><li>Iranian state media: State media denounced the players as “wartime traitors” and said authorities must deal with them severely, language supporters say heightens fears of reprisals. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/act-now-to-protect-iranian-soccer-team-australia-told/'>michaelwest.com.au</a>)</li><li>Reza Pahlavi: Pahlavi urged Australia to protect the team and said their actions could have “dire consequences,” adding to calls for asylum or other protection options. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pressure-builds-australia-offer-iran-womens-football-team-asylum'>al-monitor.com</a>)</li><li>Australian Iranian Council: The council urged Australia to let the team stay “while credible fears for their safety remain,” according to the Globe and Mail. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/sports/soccer/article-iran-soccer-team-eliminated-from-womens-asian-cup-faces-the-prospect/'>theglobeandmail.com</a>)</li><li>Australian officials (as described by advocates): Advocates said officials worry that public attention could increase risks to the players and their families. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/act-now-to-protect-iranian-soccer-team-australia-told/'>michaelwest.com.au</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/act-now-to-protect-iranian-soccer-team-australia-told/'>Act now to protect Iranian soccer team, Australia told</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pressure-builds-australia-offer-iran-womens-football-team-asylum'>Pressure builds for Australia to offer Iran women&#x27;s football team asylum</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/sports/soccer/article-iran-soccer-team-eliminated-from-womens-asian-cup-faces-the-prospect/'>Iran soccer team eliminated from Women’s Asian Cup faces the prospect of a return home</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-09/asian-cup-2026-protesters-surround-iran-team-bus/106431212'>Diaspora protesters surround the team bus of the Iranian women&#x27;s soccer team following their match against Australia amidst fears of their safety upon returning to Iran.</a> - abc.net.au</li></ul>